 "answer_raw": "Amazon has a presence in South America through localized marketplaces and international shipping, though it does not have a storefront in every country.\n\n**Brazil** is one of the countries with a dedicated Amazon marketplace, as noted in the undated dataset [8]. A large number of other countries across South America can access Amazon through **international shipping** despite lacking their own localized marketplaces [8].\n\nI didn't find which local competitors people use instead of Amazon or list every specific country with active delivery, so you would need to check local e-commerce market share reports for those details.",
